                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Seal penetrations for furnace exhaust and supply air in the basement.

Seal penetrations for electrical conduit in the basement.

Replace weather stripping and straighten exterior door frames.

Repair seal in the 72" upstairs window.

Improve sealing around the woodstove chimney penetration. Manufacturer's instructions must be followed to avoid a fire risk. An illustration will be distributed with this report to show how the air sealing may be improved here.</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>Wall insulation can be improved by adding R20 rigid foam insulation to the exterior of the walls, and replacing the fiberglass batts between the studs. This work will be elligible for a rebate of $2.50 per square foot from the Energy Solutions Centre.</mainWalls>
                <ceilings>Improving ceiling insulation to R60 by adding additional blown-in cellulose insulation will improve the house's performance, but the retrofit will not be elligible for a rebate due to the heel height. Heel height refers to the maximum insulation thickness that will fit between the attic ceiling and the wall top plate where the roof meets the wall.</ceilings>
                <exposedFloors>Adding R20 insulation to the exposed floor in the rear entryway will be elligible for a rebate of $2.50 per square foot from the energy solutions centre.</exposedFloors>
                <foundation>Foundation insulation can be improved by applying two inches of medium density spray foam to the interior of the walls.</foundation>
                <windows>The windows appear to be in good condition. However, replacing them with triple glaze, Energy Star Zone 3 windows will improve the house performance and be elligible for a rebate of $100 per window up to $1000.</windows>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
